[tool_use] Agent {"description":"QA Playwright Phase 3","subagent_type":"qa-playwright","prompt":"PointFight Reactor Phase 3 needs browser verification. Dev server runs at http://localhost:5176/.\n\nVerify the six Phase 3 acceptance criteria plus a Phase 2 regression. Phase 3 adds:\n- visuospatial SVG cues (pictographs) replacing the plain text label\n- optional text-overlay learning mode (Settings → Visuals → \"Show text label overlay\")\n- distance axis (Settings → Visuals → \"Enable distance axis\") rendering at three sizes (far/mid/in_range)\n- optional audio tone tracking distance\n- data-driven cue palette (8 cues each have an SVG pictograph and an animation)\n\nC1 — SVG pictograph per cue type\n- Start a drill with default settings. Wait through several reps. For at least 3 reps, confirm an `svg.cue-pictograph` element appears during 'showing' phase (no plain-text cue label by default). Screenshot at least 2 different cue pictographs.\n\nC2 — Optional text overlay\n- Stop. Open Settings → Visuals. Toggle ON \"Show text label overlay\". Save. Start a drill. Confirm during 'showing' the `.cue-overlay` (with the cue label text) is visible. Screenshot.\n- Toggle the overlay back OFF, save, start. Confirm the overlay is no longer visible — only the pictograph renders. Screenshot.\n\nC3 — Three distance sizes\n- Settings → Visuals → Enable distance axis. Also enable text overlay so distance labels are visible. Save. Start drill.\n- Run reps until you've seen all three distance buckets. For each, capture a screenshot and verify the inline transform: scale on `.cue-pictograph-wrap` is approximately 0.45, 0.70, and 1.0 for far/mid/in_range. The distance label text should also match.\n\nC4 — Distance changes correct response\n- Per `app/src/cues/library.ts`, when distance=far, most cues map to no-go (do_nothing). With distance axis on, fire 30+ reps WITHOUT pressing the commit key and observe that some 'far' reps end with `correct_no_go` (HOLD ✓) where the cue would have been a 'go' at mid range. Confirm by inspecting the on-screen feedback colour (green correct vs red false_start).\n\nC5 — Audio tone optional\n- Settings → enable audio tone. Save. Start drill. Run a few reps. We can't easily measure audio in a headless browser, but verify there are no console errors and the drill runs normally. Bonus: assert that an `AudioContext` exists on `window` after the drill starts (via page.evaluate).\n\nC6 — Data-driven palette\n- Inspect the runtime: page.evaluate fetching `Object.keys(window)` is not useful here. Instead, verify by DOM inspection that all 8 cue ids surface as pictographs across enough reps (set `maxReps`/long rounds). Loop until you've seen at least 6 of 8 distinct cue ids in the rendered DOM (via the SVG class names like `.cue-steps-in`, `.cue-blitzes`, etc.).\n\nPhase 2 regression\n- With ALL Phase 3 toggles OFF (default), verify a normal Phase 2 drill still: shows the round HUD, transitions through rest, hands off to Summary, recent sessions list works.\n\nReport PASS or FAIL per criterion with one-line reasons + paths to screenshots saved under `artifacts/phase3-verify/`. Track zero-console-errors throughout. Under 500 words."}
